{"id":"word:hebrew:H3899","type":"word","title":"לֶחֶם","subtitle":"H3899 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"food (for man or beast), especially bread , or grain (for making it)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לֶחֶם (H3899) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 299 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לֶחֶם (lechem) means food (for man or beast), especially bread , or grain (for making it) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 9 32."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לֶחֶם","transliteration":"lechem","pronunciation":"lekh'-em","strong":"H3899","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3899","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["לָֽחֶם","לֶ֣חֶם","לֶ֖חֶם","לֶ֔חֶם","לֶ֥חֶם"],"morphs":[["HNcbsa",153],["HNcbsc",42],["HTd/Ncbsa",16],["HRd/Ncbsa",11],["HC/Ncbsa",10],["HNcbsc/Sp1cs",8],["HNcbsc/Sp3ms",8],["HNcbsc/Sp2ms",7],["HC/Ncbsc",7],["HR/Ncbsc",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"food (for man or beast), especially bread , or grain (for making it)","usage":"(shew-) bread, × eat, food, fruit, loaf, meat, victuals.","full":"H3899. lechem לֶ֫חֶם 296 noun masculine 1Sam 9:7 and (rarely) feminine Gen 49:20 (see below, and Dr 1Sam 10:4 ) bread, food (Phoenician לחם bread ; Late Hebrew לֶחֶם ; Aramaic לַחְמָא , , as Hebrew; Arabic flesh, meat , (compare Frä 30 )); — absolute ׳ל Gen 3:19 +; לָ֑חֶם 31:54 +; לֶ֑חֶם Psa 14:4 2 t.; construct לֶחֶם Hosea 9:4 +; suffix לַחְמִי Job 3:24 +, לַחְמְךָ Obadiah 7 +, לַחְמָם Hosea 9:4 b, + 9:4 a (for לָהֶם ᵑ0 ), We GASm Now, + etc.; — 1. a. bread , the ordinary food of early Hebrews (Benz Archaeology 84 ff Now Archaeology i. 109 ff. ) Exod 21:14 (E), Num 21:5 ; Josh 9:5 , 12 (JE), Deut 8:3 ; 23:5 ; Exod 16:3 (P) +; ׳כִּכַּרלֿ loaf of bread 1Sam 2:36 + (see כִּכָּר below כרר ), and without ככר (always with number) 10:4 ; 16:20 (see Dr), 17:7 ; 21:4 ; 25:18 ; 2Sam 16:1 ; 1Kin 14:3 ; 2Kin 4:42 ; ל ׳חַלַת cake of bread 2Sam 6:19 ; Exod 29:23 + (see חַלָּה below I. חלל ); made from barley ( שְׂעֹרִים ); Judg 7:13 ; 2Kin 4:42 (see also לָחֶם above); from wheat-flour ( חִטִים סֹלֶת ) Exod 29:2 (P); compare the mixture Ezek 4:9 ; made by baking ( אפה ) Isa 44:15 , 19 ; Lev 26:26 (H; compare Jer 37:21 ); ׳מַּתלֿ a bit of bread 1Sam 2:36 ; 1Kin 17:11 ; Prov 28:21 , compare Ezek 13:19 , as modest term for a hospitable meal Gen 18:5 (J), Judg 19:5 ; 1Sam 28:22 ; distinguished from meat (flesh), Gen 27:17 (J) 1Sam 25:11 ; 1Kin 17:6 (twice in verse); Exod 16:8 , 12 (also 16:3 above), 29:32 , 34 ; Lev 8:31 (all P), 23:18 (H), 1Chr 12:40 ; Psa 78:20 ; Dan 10:3 ; = a meal 1Sam 20:27 , ל ׳אָכַל = take a meal Gen 31:54 (twice in verse); 37:25 ; 43:25 , 32 +; לַחְמִי אכל Psa 41:10 eat my bread , establishing an obligation, compare Obadiah 7 (read ל ׳אֹכְלֵי according to Marti Kau AT ; strike out ᵐ5 ׳ל Hi We, compare VB) ל ׳עשׂה = make a feast Eccl 10:19 ; ל ׳מַטֵּה staff of bread (as support of life), only late Ezek 4:16 ; 5:16 ; 14:13 ; Lev 26:26 (H), Psa 105:16 ; cf . ל ׳מִשְׁעַן Isa 3:1 (gloss); leavened bread is ׳ל חָמֵץ Lev 7:13 ; unleavened bread is ׳ל מַצּוֺת Exod 29:2 (both P); ׳ל (הַ)מָּנִים bread of the face (of ׳י ; i.e. in his presence, Di Lev 24:9 Dr 1Sam 21:7 ); in the sanctuary 21:7 ; 1Kin 7:48 2Chr 4:19 ; Exod 25:30 ; 35:13 ; 39:36 , without ׳פ 40:23 (all P); = ׳ל הַתָּמִיד Num 4:7 (P), ׳ל קֹדֶשׁ 1Sam 21:5 ; in Chronicles ׳ל הַמַּעֲרָ֑כֶת 1Chr 9:32 ; compare 23:29 ; Neh 10:34 , ׳מ ׳ל 2Chr 13:11 opposed to ׳ל חֹל 1Sam 21:5 ; ׳ל תְּנוּפִה Lev 23:17 wave-loaf ; ׳ל (הַ)בִּכֻּרִים 23:20 ; 2Kin 4:42 bread of first-fruits. b. = bread-corn , the material from which bread is made, i.e. wheat, barley, etc.: Gen 41:54-55 , (E), 47:13 , 15 , 17 (twice in verse); 47:19 (J), 49:20 (poem in J), Isa 28:28 ; 30:23 ; 55:10 ; Jer 5:17 ; Ezek 48:18 ; Job 28:5 ; Prov 28:3 ; Psa 104:14 ; ׳ל הָאָרֶץ Num 15:19 (P), ל ׳ארץ 2Kin 18:32 = Isa 36:17 . 2 food in General: a. of man , Judg 13:16 (kid, 13:15 ) 1Sam 14:24 (twice in verse); 14:28 (honey), 28:20 ; 30:12 ; Prov 22:9 ; 27:27 (twice in verse) (goat's milk) +; ל נֹתֵן ׳לְכָלבָּֿשָׂר Psa 136:25 . b. of animals , Prov 6:8 ; 30:25 ; Prov 65:25; Job 24:5 + Psa 147:9 c. of God (in sacrifices): ׳ל אֱלֹהֵיהֶם (compare RS Semitic i. 207, 2nd ed., 224 ) Lev 21:6 compare 21:8 ; 21:17 ; 21:21 ; 21:22 , 22:25 (all H), compare Num 28:2 (P), Ezek 16:19 ; 44:7 , and ׳ל מְגֹאָל Mal 1:7 , also ( ׳לי ) ׳ל אִשֶּׁה Lev 3:11 , 16 ; Num 28:24 (all P). 3 other phrases and figurative uses are: a. ׳ל רֶשַׁע Prov 4:17 (accusative of congnate meaning with verb with לָחַם ), probably = food gained by wickedness ׅ || חֲמָסִים (יִיִן , compare ׳ל שָׁ֑קֶר 20:17 , ׳ל כְּזָבִים 23:3 ; ׳ל עַצְלוּת 31:27 = bread of idleness , i.e. unearned; ׳ל חֻקִּי 30:8 (opposed to riches and poverty, see חֹק ); ׳ל לַחַץ 1Kin 22:27 2Chr 18:26 , vid לַחַץ below; ׳ל הָעֲצָבִים Psa 127:2 see II. עֶצָב ; ׳ל אוֺנִים Hosea 9:4 , vid אָוֶן . p.20 a; ׳ל אֲנָשִׁים Ezek 24:17 , 22 of food offered to mourners, compare Jer 16:7 (where insert ᵐ5 ׳ל Gf Gie); המים עלפֿני לחמך שַׁלַּח Eccl 11:1 usual interpration of benevolent giving (compare Now); De and others of sea-commerce in bread-stuffs, compare Prov 31:14 . b. figurative הֵם לַחְמֵנוּ Num 14:9 (JE) our food are they , i.e. we will devour, destroy, them (compare Deut 7:16 ); ל ׳דִּמְעָתִּי Psa 42:4 ; compare 80:6 (see אכל above); ׳ל of evil deeds of wicked Job 20:14 ; בְּלַחְמוֺ עֵץ Jer 11:19 apparentlyfig.of destroying the prophet and his house , but read probably בְּלֵחוֺ in its freshness (i.e. untimely), so Hi Gf Che Gie (see לֵחַ below לחח above).","rootNote":"from 3898 ; See also 1036","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 9 32","keyReferences":["1Chr 9 32","1Chr 12 41","1Chr 16 3","1Chr 23 29","1Kgs 5 2","1Kgs 5 23","1Kgs 7 48","1Kgs 11 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":299,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 9 32","book":"1